screens=next(ast.literal_eval(n.value) for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='SCREENS' for t in n.targets))
changes={
0:["Open ElderCareAI and tap Sign in with Google. Choose the caregiver account responsible for this patient.","Complete Google's account selection. If cancelled or unsuccessful, return to sign in and retry with internet available.","On first use, follow caregiver and patient setup. A returning account restores its saved setup and patient context.","Check the patient name on Home before viewing or recording care. Sign out through Profile before using another account.","Conceal the account email in screenshots. A saved session may bypass sign in on subsequent launches."],
1:["Enter the caregiver name, contact number, age and gender; the signed-in email identifies the account. Add a photo if desired.","Continue to the patient form and enter the older adult's name, birth date or age, gender, and the requested health details.","Add weight, height, blood type, known conditions and current medications when available. Use the displayed units.","Enter the emergency contact details and save. Correct any highlighted invalid field before continuing.","Patient selection controls the vitals, sleep, care plan, location and alerts displayed. Confirm the correct patient after changing accounts."],
2:["Open Profile and choose Connect or change watch, or continue from watch setup during onboarding.","Generate the eight-digit pairing code for the intended patient. Open ElderCareAI on the watch and enter that code.","Tap Pair watch and wait for confirmation. An invalid or expired code requires a new code; network errors require a working connection.","Confirm the phone shows Galaxy Watch6 connected. This app pairing is separate from Galaxy Wearable's Bluetooth pairing.","Allow watch sensor, activity, location and notification permissions, then start monitoring. Pair the watch again when intentionally assigning it to a different patient."],
3:["Open ElderCareAI on the paired Galaxy Watch6 and tap Start monitoring. Allow requested permissions and keep the watch snug on the wrist.","Heart rate, skin temperature, steps and HRV update when usable sensor events arrive. HRV needs a sustained interval of valid beat data and may restart after poor contact.","Location starts with monitoring. Enable Location and internet; move outdoors for better satellite reception. GPS, fused and network estimates retain source and accuracy labels.","Open Measure blood oxygen for a manual spot check. Keep the arm still. Optional five-minute auto checks work only while that screen stays open.","Inspect sharing status and queued samples. Offline vital measurements retry when connected. Tap Stop monitoring to end monitoring; restart it after a watch reboot or force stop."],
5:["Open Health and select Vitals. Review Heart Rate, Blood Oxygen, Skin Temperature, Stress level, Sleep and Steps.","Each available card shows a value, unit, status and measurement time. A status can change with a new reading; missing or stale values are not normal readings.","Heart rate, wrist temperature and valid HRV come from watch monitoring. Steps count the increments collected during monitoring on that watch day.","Blood oxygen uses spot measurements or available imported history. Sleep appears after Samsung Health records and synchronizes the patient's session.","Stress is an experimental HRV-based index. It needs a personal reference before a score is available and is not a medical diagnosis."],
6:["Tap any vital card to open its details. Read the latest value, status and original measurement time.","Scroll to Elle insight. Its observation remains steady while the live value above continues updating.","When New readings available appears, tap Refresh insight when ready. The Reading reviewed timestamp identifies the observation's reference reading.","Review recent measured history or nightly sleep entries, source details and the explanation below the card.","If the insight request fails, use Retry insight. Interpret status labels and wellness suggestions as review guidance; confirm concerns with an appropriate professional."],
8:["On the same Android phone paired to the patient's watch, install and open Samsung Health and allow its watch synchronization.","In ElderCareAI Profile, open Health History and connect the history import. Grant the requested access when prompted.","Tap Sync health history after a recorded sleep session is available. Importing sleep is different from live watch sensor monitoring.","Check the sync result and Sleep card history. No new data means no additional source records; previously saved patient history should remain available.","If access or upload fails, check internet and Samsung Health permissions and retry. Developer installations may need Samsung Health Data SDK developer access. Background checks depend on Android scheduling; wake-up delivery is not immediate."],
9:["On the watch, tap Start monitoring with Location and internet enabled. Open Live location tracking on the phone; no separate walking mode is needed.","Read the marker's source, measurement age and accuracy. The displayed stream can contain watch GPS, fused and network estimates; fused location may represent the paired phone.","Open Set up safe zone or Edit safe zone. Enter a place name, tap Choose on map and tap the actual home center, including inside the circle or on the marker.","Choose a radius from 10 to 5,000 meters, then Save and enable safe zone. Use current location can copy a fresh usable estimate; the saved center stays fixed.","An estimated exit uses 3 qualifying outside updates spanning at least 20 seconds. For a 10 or 20 m zone, reported accuracy must be 50 m or better. Larger-zone limits rise to at most 100 m.","GPS, fused and network can all confirm the marker-based crossing. Very inaccurate or stale estimates cannot. Read confirmation progress and the source-labelled alert; small-zone false alarms are possible.","Keep the zone enabled and allow background notifications. Walk outside within internet coverage and inspect Alerts. Pan to explore or tap Follow location to return; Pause alerts disables boundary checks."],
10:["Open Care plan then Medications. Tap Add to enter name, dosage, frequency and instructions from the verified prescription.","Choose an optional medication photo and review its preview. Without a photo the card uses its placeholder.","Select start and end dates and each reminder time. Displayed times use AM or PM; verify the device's local date and timezone before saving.","Save and check the medication card. Use Edit to correct the schedule; confirm Delete to remove it and cancel applicable reminders.","Tap Taken only after the dose was taken, and select the corresponding dose when asked. Watch confirmations also update the phone after successful sync; pending offline confirmations are not yet saved."],
11:["Tap Scan or upload a prescription in Care plan. Choose a clear image or capture the original with the camera.","Wait for Elle to prepare an editable draft. If extraction fails or handwriting is unclear, retry with a clearer image or enter the medication manually.","Compare every extracted name, dosage, frequency, time, instruction, date and prescriber against the original. Correct mistakes and complete missing information.","Check the review confirmation only after verification. AI extraction does not prescribe medication or verify the doctor's instruction.","Confirm and save medication. Check the resulting medication card, schedule and reminder times; unconfirmed drafts do not activate a schedule."],
12:["Open Care plan then Appointments. Tap Add and enter the purpose or title, appointment date and local time.","Add doctor name, location and notes if known. Save, correcting any invalid field while keeping the draft available.","Review the saved visit. Appointment reminders are prepared ahead of the visit; the server schedule uses a 15-minute advance, so create a test visit at least 20 minutes ahead.","Enable background notifications and check phone time and internet. A reminder is not proof the appointment has started or been attended.","Use Edit to reschedule, Complete after attendance, or confirm Delete when cancelled. The list and combined schedule refresh after the change."],
14:["Open Alerts and expand Automatic vital alerts to review the configured rules; collapse it to leave emergency actions visible.","A qualifying measured crossing saves a patient alert. The high-heart-rate warning starts above 110 BPM, rather than at 100 or exactly 110 BPM.","Open Notifications for medication, appointment and other notices. Review the timestamp and related details before acting.","Tap Enable background notifications and allow Android permission. Sound also needs the relevant channel enabled, audible volume and suitable Do Not Disturb settings.","When multiple alerts arrive together, dismiss or open the current popup to review the next queued popup. A linked-medication action is shown only when a relevant medication is associated.","Push can work when the app is backgrounded or normally closed; Android force-stop and device restrictions can prevent delivery until the app is opened again."],
15:["Save the caregiver, family member and doctor names and telephone numbers in Settings or the emergency-contact editor.","Open the emergency contact list. The order is caregiver first, family member second and doctor third.","Select a contact to open the supported phone dial action. Confirm the number before making the call.","On the watch, open SOS and tap Send SOS deliberately. Check for a successful send or a pending/error message; merely opening the screen does not send it.","Review the saved SOS in the phone Emergency tab, then acknowledge or respond through the alert actions. An SOS does not automatically call emergency services."],
17:["Open Profile to review the active caregiver, patient and Galaxy Watch6 connection. Edit the relevant profile or emergency contacts as needed.","Use Health History to connect and import recorded sleep and supported overnight oxygen. Keep the patient's paired-watch identity correct.","Select Health vitals PDF or Medication schedule PDF. The export uses saved records for the selected patient and opens the supported sharing options.","If a required record is missing or an export fails, check patient selection, connectivity and the displayed message before retrying.","Enable background notifications from Alerts. Sign out before switching caregiver accounts and check the restored patient after the next sign-in."],
18:["Open the website's administrator portal and sign in with an authorized administrator username or email and password.","If sign-in fails, correct the credentials; use Forgot password and follow its verification steps when recovery is needed.","Overview displays saved system counts, recent alerts and emergency activity. Refresh to request updated administration data.","In Accounts select a caregiver and review the linked patients. Use permitted editing and access controls and read each confirmation before saving a change.","Use Install or try the app on the public landing page to open the Android APK and installation instructions. The caregiver phone app uses its own Google sign-in."],
19:["Open System monitor to inspect reported connection state and recent database health syncs. This is not a live watch sensor display.","Distinguish Saved at, the database write time, from Measured at, the original measurement time. Older saved readings do not establish current sensor activity.","Open Alerts and notifications to review saved warnings and emergency history, including status and delivery information.","Open Reports, choose report type and date range, then generate the available CSV. Review empty results and errors before retrying.","Use Security for supported administrator access and audit tasks. Sign out when finished, and hide personal identifiers in screenshots."],
}
for index,bullets in changes.items():
 title,route,shot,_=screens[index]
 if index==3:shot='Capture Start monitoring or Stop monitoring, current readings, Location and sharing status.'
 screens[index]=(title,route,shot,bullets)
extra={4:["Tap Sync now or pull to refresh when needed. A failed refresh should not be mistaken for a new measurement.","Tap a vital card for detail or a care task to open its relevant Care plan screen."],7:["Use actual measurement timestamps to distinguish delayed uploads from newly measured values.","If the range is empty, choose a date with saved readings. Retry a failed load instead of assuming a zero value."],13:["Reschedule a visit or edit a dose time and reopen Schedule to check its new chronological position.","For simultaneous reminders, verify both separate items remain visible and capture both popups after dismissing each in turn."],16:["Wait for the thinking indicator to finish. If a service error appears, retry while connected.","Use related-screen actions or evidence links when offered. Start New Chat for a separate question."]}
for index,items in extra.items():
 title,route,shot,bullets=screens[index];screens[index]=(title,route,shot,bullets+items)

